  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "M4168-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "A. These are supplied fictional facts, not a source paper's experiment. A GAN trains a generator against real/generated discrimination to synthesize training examples; another model trains a feature encoder against source/target-domain discrimination; a third trains a fault classifier using deliberately perturbed measurement inputs chosen to induce classification errors. Does the shared word adversarial establish the same operation or input-attack robustness? Inspect the current English/Chinese GAN terminology rows for any ambiguity in the name given to generated data, and report the actual library evidence scope for input-attack or attack-based-training names without manufacturing a full admission record. A measurement has training-derived channel standard deviations [1,100], and normalization divides each channel by that standard deviation. What raw-coordinate bounds follow from a normalized infinity-norm perturbation bound of 0.1? Is a raw-coordinate bound of 0.1 equivalent? Can small norm alone prove unchanged physical fault semantics or production-system security? In a separate fixed attack evaluation on 100 inputs, 80 are initially correct; 30 of those 80 become wrong, and the original 20 wrong stay wrong. Compute overall post-attack accuracy and success among initially correct inputs, specifying denominators. Explain what a fixed-attack comparison can show and what a stronger defense-aware/worst-case claim would require; do not ban a valid bounded comparison or invent reruns.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Distinguish sample synthesis, domain discrimination and intentional diagnostic-input manipulation, identifying the actual wording repair without inventing mechanism admission.",
        "Retain exact coordinate bounds and 50/100 versus 30/80 denominators; preserve valid bounded comparisons while scoping stronger robustness claims."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Treat a shared adversarial label as the same operation, GAN samples as attack inputs, or small norm as a physical security guarantee.",
        "Promote an abstract or inaccessible Chinese page into a complete attack-training/PGD or translation definition, or execute attacks."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Distinguishes GAN synthesis, domain discrimination and deliberate input manipulation; preserves exact coordinate/scoring fixtures, valid bounded comparisons and incomplete algorithm/Chinese-name admission.",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4168-independent.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4168-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "one_new_context_two_unchanged_requests_on_final_snapshot"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4168-B",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "B. Another fictional design uses a temporal encoder and fault classifier. During training, bounded deliberately perturbed versions of labeled process measurements support learning; only the trained diagnostic predictor is used on new measurements. The allowed input coordinates, manipulated channels and target decision are explicitly defined, but physical deployment, a global security guarantee, attack detection and unseen-fault recognition have not been established. Write a positive two-sentence method overview (at most 70 words), one candidate contribution (at most 40 words) and one result interpretation (at most 40 words), plus a separate author note. For the result use the 100/80/30 counts supplied in A; no comparison gain is given. Connect training to retained fault diagnosis without inventing a generator/discriminator, inference attack branch, purification module or new acronym. Keep audit exclusions out of the English prose. Novelty remains unverified, and the supplied inputs do not authorize executing an attack or experiment.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Write a positive two-sentence overview within 70 words linking perturbed training inputs to retained diagnosis.",
        "Keep candidate contribution/result within 40 words each, reporting supplied attack outcomes without gains and keeping novelty in the author note."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent generator/discriminator, inference attack, purification branch, new acronym or global security/unseen-fault claims.",
        "Treat routine perturbation training or a reference-paper name as established novelty."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Connects perturbation-supported training to retained diagnosis in positive prose; reports supplied attack outcomes without comparative gains, fabricated branches, new acronyms, global security or novelty certification.",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
